:"}]},{"code":["<key>keychain-access-groups<\/key>","<array>","    <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.example.myapp<\/string>","<\/array>"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"xml"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS \/ iPadOS \/ tvOS \/ watchOS only have the data-protection keychain and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"supply the access group implicitly — no extra entitlement is required."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Which-entitlement-for-privacy","text":"Which entitlement, for privacy"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Encryption, this-device-only accessibility, iCloud-sync exclusion, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backup exclusion are identical whichever path you take — the access group"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only governs "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which of your own apps"}]},{"type":"text","text":" can read an item, never third"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parties or the cloud. For app-private identifiers, in order of strictness:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Most private:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" a provisioning-profile–signed build with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"accessGroup: nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", relying on the implicit "},{"code":"application-identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"group ("},{"code":"<TeamPrefix>.<bundle-id>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). No other app — even one you sign"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under the same team — can ever be entitled to it. Mirrors the iOS"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default exactly; zero sharing surface."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Practically equivalent:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" a "},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" array whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"only","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" entry is the team-prefixed bundle id (the snippet above). Use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this when a profile-signed build isn’t available (unsigned local \/ CI"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dev, where −34018 bites). The one delta from (1): another app you sign"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under the same team could also declare that string and read the items."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Intentional sharing only:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" a deliberately shared group string. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"first","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" element of "},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes the default group"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for new items, so never put a shared group first for private data."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Sendable","text":"Sendable"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Marked "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@unchecked Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Security"},{"type":"text","text":" framework’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SecItem*"},{"type":"text","text":" calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are thread-safe; the struct’s stored properties are all themselves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" or treated so. Matches the pattern of "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux